---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Who writes powerbitutorials.com, how every tutorial is verified in Power BI Desktop, and how to report an error."
  article={true}
>
  <article class="about-page">
    <div class="content-width">
      <span class="page-eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1>Practical Power BI tutorials, written by one person</h1>

      <p class="lede">
        powerbitutorials.com is an independent tutorial site about Power BI, DAX and Power Query.
        It is written and maintained by Mireia, and it has no connection to Microsoft.
      </p>

      <h2>What this site is for</h2>
      <p>
        Most Power BI material sits at one of two extremes: short listicles that never show a working
        model, or reference documentation that explains syntax without saying when you would actually
        use it. This site aims at the space in between — one specific problem per article, a model you
        can rebuild, and an explanation of <em>why</em> the formula behaves the way it does.
      </p>
      <p>
        The measure of a good tutorial here is simple: after reading it, you should be able to adapt
        the solution to your own data instead of copying it and hoping.
      </p>

      <h2>How each tutorial is made</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Topics come from problems, not keywords.</strong> They are drawn from questions that
          recur in search results, forum threads and reader email — the places where people get stuck
          on the same thing again and again.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Every formula is run before it is published.</strong> DAX and Power Query snippets
          are tested against a sample model in Power BI Desktop. If a measure does not return the
          stated result, it does not ship. Where behaviour depends on version or storage mode, the
          article says so explicitly.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Articles are dated and re-checked.</strong> Each tutorial shows when it was published
          and when it was last reviewed. Power BI changes — visuals get renamed, preview features
          graduate, older functions get superseded — and articles are revised rather than left to
          drift out of date.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Version-dependent claims link to Microsoft.</strong> Anything that could change under
          you is linked to the official documentation so you can verify it yourself rather than take
          this site's word for it.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Technical sites get things wrong, and a tutorial that is quietly incorrect is worse than no
        tutorial at all. If you find an error, a formula that does not work on your model, or a step
        that assumes something you don't have, <a href="/contact">tell me</a> — corrections are
        applied and the review date is updated. Reader reports are the main way this site improves.
      </p>

      <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Microsoft.</li>
        <li>
          No tool or course is recommended because someone paid for it. Where an affiliate link
          appears, it is disclosed on that page.
        </li>
        <li>There is no account, no paywall and no email required to read anything here.</li>
        <li>
          No tutorial is published on a fixed daily schedule to hit a quota. Coverage follows what
          readers actually need.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who writes it</h2>

      <!-- TODO(author): replace this paragraph with 2-3 sentences of real background
           (years with Power BI, the models you build, where you hit these problems).
           Do not overstate — reviewers check. Do not name an employer. -->
      <p>
        Mireia builds Power BI models and writes about the parts that took longest to get right —
        filter context, context transition, and why a measure that looks correct returns the wrong
        number. Every article on this site is written and maintained by the same person, which is
        why the explanations stay consistent from one tutorial to the next.
      </p>

      <div class="author-card">
        <div class="author-avatar" aria-hidden="true">M</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Mireia</h3>
          <p>
            Author and maintainer of powerbitutorials.com.
            <a href="/contact">Get in touch</a> — every message is read.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>How the site is funded</h2>
      <p>
        This site is free to read and does not require an account. If it saves you time, the most
        useful thing you can do is send the article to a colleague who is stuck on the same problem.
      </p>

      <div class="about-cta">
        <a href="/tutorials" class="btn btn-primary">Browse tutorials</a>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-secondary">Contact</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page { padding: 56px 0 80px; }
  .page-eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--c-accent);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .about-page h1 {
    font-size: 2.4rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--c-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--c-accent);
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  .about-page h2 { margin-top: 2.5em; }
  .about-page ol, .about-page ul { padding-left: 1.4em; }
  .about-page li { margin-bottom: 0.7em; }
  .author-card {
    display: flex;
    gap: 18px;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 20px;
    background: var(--c-bg-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    margin: 28px 0;
  }
  .author-avatar {
    width: 56px;
    height: 56px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--c-accent);
    color: var(--c-accent-text);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-weight: 800;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .author-card h3 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .author-card p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.92rem; }
  .about-cta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
  .btn {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 11px 22px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 0.15s ease;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
  }
  .btn-primary { background: var(--c-accent); color: var(--c-accent-text); }
  .btn-primary:hover { background: var(--c-accent-hover); text-decoration: none; }
  .btn-secondary { background: var(--c-bg); color: var(--c-text); border-color: var(--c-border); }
  .btn-secondary:hover { border-color: var(--c-accent); color: var(--c-accent); text-decoration: none; }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .about-page h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; }
    .author-card { flex-direction: column; text-align: center; }
    .about-cta { flex-direction: column; }
  }
</style>
